# Byte-exact storage, everywhere.
#
# Every published hash in this project is SHA-256 over file bytes read from disk
# (`tools/validate_results_v2.py`, the config freshness assertions in
# `tests/test_divinity_ontology.py`, `preregistration.mechanism.operator_cost_table_sha256`),
# and this working tree mixes CRLF and LF. Git's default line-ending handling
# (`core.autocrlf=true` on Windows) rewrites those bytes at checkout: the committed
# blobs would land as LF on one machine and CRLF on another, and a clone would then
# report every hashed artifact as stale. That is a reproducibility failure caused by
# the transport, not by the data, so the conversion is switched off and the
# repository stores exactly the bytes that produced the published hashes.
* -text
